# Build output.
bin/

# npm is DEV-TIME ONLY: `just assets` installs here to build the editor bundle,
# and the BUILT internal/serve/assets/editor.{js,css} are committed — so a
# checkout with no node on it still serves the editor. Deliberately no rule for
# those two files: nothing here may ignore them.
web/node_modules/

# The running editor's advert beside a document (`galley edit` writes
# <doc>.serve.json and removes it on exit). It belongs to a session, not the
# repo.
*.serve.json

# THE HISTORY IS LOCAL INSURANCE, NOT A SHARED ARTIFACT — the spec's own
# framing. `.galley/versions/<doc>/` holds a FULL COPY of the document per
# round, beside the reviewer's file, and `galley edit` starts writing them the
# moment it opens one; committed by default that is a live hour's forty copies
# of somebody's draft arriving in a pull request. Not like the ledger, which is
# one line per decision and is deliberately committed — `.galley/decisions.jsonl`
# at the repo root stays tracked and is NOT covered by this rule. A team that
# wants a shared history un-ignores this deliberately.
**/.galley/versions/

# THE PAGE ARTIFACTS ARE DERIVED, NOT AUTHORED — same logic as versions above.
# `.galley/pages/<base>/` holds what `galley page` extracted from an HTML file:
# content.md, template.json and original.html, all regenerable from the source
# page. Committed by default that is a second copy of the page arriving in a
# pull request. A team that wants them shared un-ignores this deliberately.
**/.galley/pages/

# Worktrees live inside the repo, at .worktrees/<name>. The coordination clone
# is bare so git never looks at them there — this is for the case where it is
# not, so a checkout never reports every other branch as untracked files.
.worktrees/

# Tooling scratch.
.playwright-mcp/
.skylos/
.golangci-cache/

# Bare `go build ./cmd/galley-mint` drops binary at repo root; ignore it.
/galley-mint

# Design docs never live in this public repo: specs and plans are in private tools-ops (docs/<repo>/).
docs/specs/
docs/plans/
docs/superpowers/
